<%# The newsletter row's modals, registered into the page's scoped host.

    Locals: user (required).

    BOTH CARRY THE FORM THEY SUBMIT, so there is exactly one place each verb is
    issued from. A confirmation whose button posts a form elsewhere on the page
    drifts the moment that form moves.

      newsletter-unsubscribe — the confirmation. DELETE.
      newsletter-email       — the address capture, for an account with none on
                               file. POST, with the address in the same request.

    The email modal exists because a wallet-only account (turf-monster has many)
    has no address, and a newsletter needs somewhere to send. It is written as the
    account email but NOT marked verified — see the controller for why that
    distinction is load-bearing.

    FOR A HOST THAT MOUNTS THESE ITSELF (turf-monster, on its own $store.modals
    and its own JSON routes). Every local below is optional, and with all of them
    unset the two cards above render byte for byte as they did before the locals
    existed (test/views/newsletter_modals_test.rb holds that).

      modal_store       the Alpine store the cards answer to. Default
                        "profileModals"; validated as a JS identifier, since
                        it is spliced as a name ($store.<name>.close()).
      submit_mode       :form (default) — each card posts the engine form to
                        profile_newsletter_path with Turbo off, a full reload.
                        :json — each card posts JSON to the host's route
                        (studio/newsletter_modal), stays on the page, shows a
                        spinner and an inline error line, dispatches
                        changed_event and steps to the next card. A card whose
                        opener passed props.onSubmit hands it the address and
                        posts nothing: the opener's own request takes over.
      subscribe_url     :json only, and required there by every card that
                        subscribes (email, subscribe). The host's endpoint.
      unsubscribe_url   :json only, and required there by the unsubscribe card.
      unsubscribe_method :json only. The verb the unsubscribe card sends.
                        Default "DELETE", the engine route's.
      changed_event     :json only. The window event a success dispatches,
                        with { subscribed, email, response }. Default
                        "studio:newsletter-changed".

    THE CARDS. Each is a Hash of its copy, or off. The two above are on by
    default (false turns one off); the other three are off by default (a Hash,
    or true for the engine's copy, turns one on). Every card takes id:, title:,
    subtitle: and header: (more blocks/_card_header locals: size, icon,
    icon_emoji, icon_color), plus the keys listed. An unknown key raises.

      unsubscribe_card  'newsletter-unsubscribe'. button:, cancel:, saving:.
                        :json steps to goodbye_card when it is on.
      email_card        'newsletter-email'. button:, cancel:, saving:.
                        :json steps to success_card when it is on.
      subscribe_card    'newsletter-subscribe'. The join, with a consent box
                        (ticked to start; Subscribe waits for it) and, for an
                        account with no address, the address field. consent:,
                        button:, cancel:, saving:. :json steps to success_card.
      success_card      'newsletter-success'. The "Subscribed!" beat. partial:
                        and locals: render the host's slot under the header (a
                        seeds bar, a next-step button); the card's props, the
                        host's JSON answer, are in scope there as `props`. With
                        no slot the card ends in a Close button; with one, a
                        Close link (cancel:).
      goodbye_card      'newsletter-goodbye'. The beat after an unsubscribe.
                        button:.
%>
<%
  newsletter_modal_store = Studio::JsIdentifier.validate!(
    local_assigns.fetch(:modal_store, "profileModals"), local: :modal_store)
  newsletter_mode = local_assigns.fetch(:submit_mode, :form).to_sym
  unless %i[form json].include?(newsletter_mode)
    raise ArgumentError, "studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals submit_mode: :form or :json, got #{newsletter_mode.inspect}"
  end
  newsletter_json = newsletter_mode == :json

  # Each card's defaults; a host's Hash is merged over them. The two cards that
  # shipped first keep their copy and their header exactly.
  newsletter_card_defaults = {
    unsubscribe_card: { on: true, id: "newsletter-unsubscribe",
                        title: "Unsubscribe?",
                        subtitle: "You'll stop receiving updates. You can join again from this page any time.",
                        header: { size: :lg, icon: :error },
                        button: "Unsubscribe", cancel: "Cancel", saving: "Unsubscribing…" },
    email_card:       { on: true, id: "newsletter-email",
                        title: "Where should we send it?",
                        subtitle: "There's no email on this account yet. We'll use this for the newsletter.",
                        header: { size: :lg, icon_color: :primary },
                        button: "Subscribe", cancel: "Cancel", saving: "Subscribing…" },
    subscribe_card:   { on: false, id: "newsletter-subscribe",
                        title: "Join the newsletter",
                        subtitle: "News and updates, now and then. Leave any time.",
                        header: { size: :md, icon_emoji: "📬" },
                        consent: "Send me the newsletter",
                        button: "Subscribe", cancel: "Close", saving: "Subscribing…" },
    success_card:     { on: false, id: "newsletter-success",
                        title: "Subscribed!",
                        subtitle: "You're on the list.",
                        header: { size: :lg, icon_emoji: "🎉" },
                        partial: nil, locals: {},
                        button: "Close", cancel: "Close" },
    goodbye_card:     { on: false, id: "newsletter-goodbye",
                        title: "See you later",
                        subtitle: "You're off the list. You can join again any time.",
                        header: { size: :lg, icon_emoji: "👋" },
                        button: "Close" }
  }

  newsletter_cards = newsletter_card_defaults.to_h do |name, defaults|
    given = local_assigns.fetch(name) { defaults[:on] }
    card = case given
           when false, nil then nil
           when true then defaults
           when Hash
             unknown = given.keys - (defaults.keys - [:on])
             if unknown.any?
               raise ArgumentError, "studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals #{name}: unknown key #{unknown.map(&:inspect).join(', ')}"
             end
             defaults.merge(given).merge(header: defaults[:header].merge(given[:header] || {}))
           else
             raise ArgumentError, "studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals #{name}: a Hash, true or false, got #{given.inspect}"
           end
    [name, card]
  end

  # The URL each JSON card posts to, refused at render when missing: a card with
  # no endpoint renders perfectly and fails on the one press that matters.
  newsletter_url = lambda do |key|
    url = local_assigns[key].presence
    raise ArgumentError, "studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals: submit_mode: :json needs #{key}" unless url
    url
  end

  # The x-data for one JSON card (studio/newsletter_modal). Every value lands in
  # a JS string, escaped; tag.attributes encodes the double quote.
  newsletter_scope = lambda do |**opts|
    pairs = { store: newsletter_modal_store }.merge(opts).map do |key, value|
      literal = (value == true || value == false) ? value.to_s : "'#{Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(value.to_s)}'"
      "#{key}: #{literal}"
    end
    "studioNewsletterModal({ #{pairs.join(', ')} })".html_safe
  end

  newsletter_needs_email = Studio::Newsletter.needs_email?(user)
  newsletter_success_id  = newsletter_cards[:success_card]&.dig(:id).to_s
  newsletter_goodbye_id  = newsletter_cards[:goodbye_card]&.dig(:id).to_s
  newsletter_changed     = local_assigns.fetch(:changed_event, "studio:newsletter-changed")
%>

<%# --- leaving asks --------------------------------------------------------- %>
<% if (card = newsletter_cards[:unsubscribe_card]) %>
<template x-if="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.current()?.id === '<%= Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(card[:id]) %>'">
  <div<% if newsletter_json %> <%= tag.attributes("x-data": newsletter_scope.call(action: "unsubscribe", url: newsletter_url.call(:unsubscribe_url), method: local_assigns.fetch(:unsubscribe_method, "DELETE"), nextId: newsletter_goodbye_id, event: newsletter_changed)) %><% end %>>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
          **card[:header], title: card[:title], subtitle: card[:subtitle] %>

<% if newsletter_json %>
    <p x-show="error" x-cloak role="alert" aria-live="assertive" aria-atomic="true"
       x-text="error" class="text-xs mb-3 text-center text-danger-ink"></p>
    <button type="button" @click="submit()" :disabled="!ready"
            class="btn btn-danger btn-lg w-full disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
      <span x-show="!saving"><%= card[:button] %></span>
      <span x-show="saving" x-cloak class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true" style="--spinner-track: currentColor; --spinner-color: transparent; opacity: 0.85"></span><%= card[:saving] %>
      </span>
    </button>
<% else %>
    <%= form_with url: profile_newsletter_path, method: :delete, data: { turbo: false } do %>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger btn-lg w-full"><%= card[:button] %></button>
    <% end %>
<% end %>

    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()"
            class="block mx-auto mt-3 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition">
      <%= card[:cancel] %>
    </button>
  </div>
</template>
<% end %>

<%# --- joining without an address on file ----------------------------------- %>
<% if (card = newsletter_cards[:email_card]) %>
<template x-if="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.current()?.id === '<%= Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(card[:id]) %>'">
  <div<% if newsletter_json %> <%= tag.attributes("x-data": newsletter_scope.call(action: "subscribe", url: newsletter_url.call(:subscribe_url), needsEmail: true, nextId: newsletter_success_id, event: newsletter_changed)) %><% end %>>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
          **card[:header], title: card[:title], subtitle: card[:subtitle] %>

<% if newsletter_json %>
    <input type="email" x-model="email" @keydown.enter.prevent="submit()" required autocomplete="email"
           placeholder="you@example.com" class="input-field w-full mb-3">
    <p x-show="error" x-cloak role="alert" aria-live="assertive" aria-atomic="true"
       x-text="error" class="text-xs mb-3 text-danger-ink"></p>
    <button type="button" @click="submit()" :disabled="!ready"
            class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
      <span x-show="!saving"><%= card[:button] %></span>
      <span x-show="saving" x-cloak class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true" style="--spinner-track: currentColor; --spinner-color: transparent; opacity: 0.85"></span><%= card[:saving] %>
      </span>
    </button>
<% else %>
    <%= form_with url: profile_newsletter_path, method: :post, scope: :profile,
                  data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
      <%= f.email_field :email, required: true, autocomplete: "email",
                        placeholder: "you@example.com",
                        class: "input-field w-full mb-3" %>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full"><%= card[:button] %></button>
    <% end %>
<% end %>

    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()"
            class="block mx-auto mt-3 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition">
      <%= card[:cancel] %>
    </button>
  </div>
</template>
<% end %>
<%# --- joining, with consent (optional) ------------------------------------ %>
<% if (card = newsletter_cards[:subscribe_card]) %>

<template x-if="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.current()?.id === '<%= Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(card[:id]) %>'">
  <div <%= tag.attributes("x-data": newsletter_scope.call(**(newsletter_json ? { action: "subscribe", url: newsletter_url.call(:subscribe_url), needsEmail: newsletter_needs_email, requiresConsent: true, nextId: newsletter_success_id, event: newsletter_changed } : {}))) %>>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
          **card[:header], title: card[:title], subtitle: card[:subtitle] %>

<% if newsletter_json %>
    <% if newsletter_needs_email %>
    <input type="email" x-model="email" @keydown.enter.prevent="submit()" required autocomplete="email"
           placeholder="you@example.com" class="input-field w-full mb-3">
    <% end %>
    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-secondary mb-3 select-none cursor-pointer">
      <input type="checkbox" x-model="consent" class="rounded border-subtle text-primary cursor-pointer">
      <%= card[:consent] %>
    </label>
    <p x-show="error" x-cloak role="alert" aria-live="assertive" aria-atomic="true"
       x-text="error" class="text-xs mb-3 text-danger-ink"></p>
    <button type="button" @click="submit()" :disabled="!ready"
            class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed">
      <span x-show="!saving"><%= card[:button] %></span>
      <span x-show="saving" x-cloak class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
        <span class="spinner" aria-hidden="true" style="--spinner-track: currentColor; --spinner-color: transparent; opacity: 0.85"></span><%= card[:saving] %>
      </span>
    </button>
<% else %>
    <%# The plain path: the browser holds the submit until the box is ticked. %>
    <%= form_with url: profile_newsletter_path, method: :post, scope: :profile,
                  data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
      <% if newsletter_needs_email %>
      <%= f.email_field :email, required: true, autocomplete: "email",
                        placeholder: "you@example.com",
                        class: "input-field w-full mb-3" %>
      <% end %>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-secondary mb-3 select-none cursor-pointer">
        <input type="checkbox" required checked class="rounded border-subtle text-primary cursor-pointer">
        <%= card[:consent] %>
      </label>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full"><%= card[:button] %></button>
    <% end %>
<% end %>

    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()"
            class="block mx-auto mt-3 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition">
      <%= card[:cancel] %>
    </button>
  </div>
</template>
<% end %>
<%# --- the "Subscribed!" beat (optional) ------------------------------------ %>
<% if (card = newsletter_cards[:success_card]) %>

<template x-if="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.current()?.id === '<%= Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(card[:id]) %>'">
  <div <%= tag.attributes("x-data": newsletter_scope.call) %>>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
          **card[:header], title: card[:title], subtitle: card[:subtitle] %>

<% if card[:partial] %>
    <%= render card[:partial], **(card[:locals] || {}) %>

    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()"
            class="block mx-auto mt-3 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition">
      <%= card[:cancel] %>
    </button>
<% else %>
    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full">
      <%= card[:button] %>
    </button>
<% end %>
  </div>
</template>
<% end %>
<%# --- the goodbye beat (optional) ----------------------------------------- %>
<% if (card = newsletter_cards[:goodbye_card]) %>

<template x-if="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.current()?.id === '<%= Studio::JsLiteral.in_attribute(card[:id]) %>'">
  <div <%= tag.attributes("x-data": newsletter_scope.call) %>>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/card_header",
          **card[:header], title: card[:title], subtitle: card[:subtitle] %>

    <button type="button" @click="$store.<%= newsletter_modal_store %>.close()" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full">
      <%= card[:button] %>
    </button>
  </div>
</template>
<% end %>
